# Tech Stack & Architecture Overview

## Overview

This application is a personal financial management platform with an enterprise mindset, where users manage their finances as if they were running a company.

The system is designed to provide:

- Full financial control
- Strategic analysis
- Intelligent insights generation
- Scalability for AI and automation

## Architectural Principles

- Backend-driven logic: all business rules must reside in the backend
- Separation of concerns: clear and well-defined layers
- Data-first approach: decisions driven by data
- Scalability by design: built to grow
- Intelligence-ready: prepared for analytics and AI

## Frontend

### Stack

- React
- Vite
- TypeScript
- TailwindCSS
- React Hook Form
- Zod

### Responsibilities

- User interface (UI/UX)
- Data input handling
- Form validation
- API consumption

### Best Practices

- Never implement financial logic on the frontend
- Use Zod integrated with React Hook Form for validation
- Prioritize component reusability and modularity

## Backend

### Stack

- Node.js
- NestJS

### Responsibilities

- Business logic
- Financial processing
- API exposure (REST or GraphQL)
- Authentication and authorization
- Orchestration of analytics

### Recommended Structure

```text
/src
  /modules
    /transactions
    /accounts
    /debts
    /investments
  /domain
    /services
    /rules
  /analytics
    /services
    /jobs
  /infra
    /database
    /queue
```

## Database

### Technology

- PostgreSQL

### Justification

- Supports complex queries
- Strong relational consistency
- Ideal for financial analytics
- Scalable and reliable

## ORM

### Technology

- Prisma

### Responsibilities

- Object-relational mapping
- Versioned migrations
- Strong typing with TypeScript

## Infrastructure

### Platform

- Render

### Recommended Setup

- Service 1: API (backend)
- Service 2: Worker (jobs/cron processing)
- Database: Managed PostgreSQL

## Intelligence Layer

### Objective

Transform financial data into actionable insights.

### Analysis Services

Responsible for interpreting financial data:

- FinancialAnalysisService
- BehaviorAnalysisService
- TrendAnalysisService

### Jobs (Asynchronous Processing)

Executed periodically:

- Daily analysis
- Monthly consolidation
- Metrics calculation
- Alert generation

### Structure

```text
/analytics
  /jobs
    daily-analysis.job.ts
    monthly-summary.job.ts
  /services
    financial-analysis.service.ts
    behavior.service.ts
```

## Financial Domain

### Core Entities

- Transactions (income and expenses)
- Categories
- Accounts
- Debts
- Investments

### Applied Concepts

- Income = revenue
- Expenses = operational costs
- Profit = net result
- Debt = liabilities
- Investments = capital allocation

## Key Metrics (KPIs)

- Monthly net profit
- Savings rate
- Debt ratio
- Total net worth
- Personal burn rate

## Critical Rules

- No financial logic should exist in the frontend
- All metrics must be calculated in the backend
- Data must be stored with historical tracking (time-series)
- Avoid duplication of business logic

## Future Evolution

- Open Finance integration
- Personal financial scoring system
- AI-driven recommendation engine
- Autonomous financial agents
- Scenario simulation (what-if analysis)

## Summary

This stack is designed to ensure:

- High scalability
- Clear architecture
- Advanced analytical capability
- Strong foundation for AI-driven features

This document should be used as a standard baseline for all future related projects.
